Makedonka Cursive — License
============================

This font, "Makedonka Cursive" (Regular and Bold), (C) 2026 Goran Arsov, is a
DERIVATIVE WORK of:

    "Macedonian cursive script" by MacedonianBoy (Wikimedia Commons)
    https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Macedonian_cursive_script.svg
    Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC BY-SA 3.0).

The letterforms were vectorized (traced) from that chart. The digits, the punctuation,
the Bold weight, the full Latin alphabet, and the spacing/kerning/engineering are
additions by Goran Arsov (the font's author). Changes were made to the original material.

Because it derives from a CC BY-SA 3.0 work, this font is itself licensed under:

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC BY-SA 3.0)

    Full legal text:        https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/legalcode
    Human-readable summary:  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

You are free to:
  * Share  — copy and redistribute the font in any medium or format.
  * Adapt  — remix, transform, and build upon it.
  * for any purpose, including commercially.

Under the following terms:
  * Attribution — You must give appropriate credit to "MacedonianBoy" (original cursive
    letterforms), provide a link to the CC BY-SA 3.0 license, and indicate that changes
    were made. You may do so in any reasonable manner (a credits/colophon/about page, or
    a comment in the CSS, is enough). Attribution is also embedded in the font's
    name-table metadata.
  * ShareAlike — If you remix, transform, or build upon the font, you must distribute your
    contributions under the same license (CC BY-SA 3.0). The font CANNOT be made
    proprietary or distributed under closed/restrictive terms; anyone who receives it
    receives these same freedoms.
  * No additional restrictions — You may not apply legal terms or technological measures
    that legally restrict others from doing anything the license permits.

Note on selling: you may charge money for this font, but doing so does not change the
license — buyers still receive it under CC BY-SA 3.0 (they may redistribute and modify it,
and must ShareAlike). To license a font under proprietary/closed terms, the letterforms
would have to be drawn from scratch rather than traced from the CC BY-SA 3.0 source.

This file is a practical summary for convenience; the full license text (linked above) is
the governing legal document. This is not legal advice.
